{
  "info": {
    "name": "KNOX API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Curated requests for the KNOX API, in the order you would use them. Run them top to bottom the first time: each request stores the ids and tokens the next ones need (collection variables).\n\nSetup\n1. Start the local stack (see KNOX README, \"Run everything locally\").\n2. Import this collection and `KNOX.local.postman_environment.json`, then select the \"KNOX local\" environment.\n3. Run \"Auth / Log in (admin)\". Every other request sends the stored token automatically (collection-level Bearer auth).\n\nGood to know\n- Errors are RFC 7807 problem details: `detail` explains, `code` identifies business errors, `errors` lists validation failures. Every response carries a `traceId` you can find in the API logs.\n- Log in/register are rate limited (5 per minute per IP). A 429 means wait a minute.\n- The full, always-current endpoint list with schemas is the OpenAPI document: {{apiUrl}}/openapi/v1.json (Swagger UI at {{apiUrl}}/swagger). Postman can import it too.\n- Course files: \"Materials\" shows the direct-upload flow. Step 2 sends the file straight to object storage with the presigned URL from step 1; the API never receives the bytes."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "majorId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "universityId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "facultyId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "courseId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "folderId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadKey",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadUrl",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "uploadContentType",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "materialId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "quizId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "jobId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Readiness (through the proxy)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthz",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "healthz"
              ]
            },
            "description": "200 `Healthy` when the API can reach SQL Server and object storage (what uptime monitors call).",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Log in (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signs in and stores accessToken/refreshToken for the other requests. The seeded SuperAdmin comes from SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL/SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD (.env.local).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const tokens = body.tokens ?? body; // register nests them, login/refresh/verify return them directly",
                  "if (tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Who am I",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The caller's profile, role and academic affiliation. Stores majorId for later requests."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"majorId\", body.majorId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register a student",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a User-role account. Returns tokens right away unless REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=true (then `requiresVerification` is true and a code is emailed; without an email provider the code is printed in the API log). Stores the new user's id as userId (the admin session stays active).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"student.{{$timestamp}}@knox.local\",\n  \"password\": \"Student123\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Test Student\",\n  \"majorId\": {{majorId}}\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "// Keep the admin session: only remember who was created (the Administration requests act on this user).",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userId\", pm.response.json().user.domainUserId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh tokens",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges the refresh token for a new pair. Refresh tokens are single-use: sending an old one again revokes all of the user's sessions.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const tokens = body.tokens ?? body; // register nests them, login/refresh/verify return them directly",
                  "if (tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Send verification / reset code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-verification-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "send-verification-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Emails a 6-digit code (account verification or password reset). 204 on success; 409 `OTP.NotSent` when throttled or the address is unknown.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Log out",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Revokes this refresh token (no access token needed). Send an empty body while signed in to sign out everywhere.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Account (run manually)",
      "description": "Requests that change state or need input from you; the rest of the collection runs top to bottom without them.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Change password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "change-password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Changes the signed-in user's password: 204. The new password must differ from the current one and have 8+ characters with upper, lower and a digit. Update adminPassword in the environment afterwards.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"{{adminPassword}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"Replace-Me-1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-account",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "verify-account"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only needed when REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=true: put the registered email and the 6-digit code (from the email, or the API log without an email provider). Returns tokens.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"student@example.com\",\n  \"otp\": \"123456\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const tokens = body.tokens ?? body; // register nests them, login/refresh/verify return them directly",
                  "if (tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", tokens.refreshToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
